.TH WDRAFT 1 2026-10-03 "wdraft 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
wdraft \- drag-and-drop source/sink for Wayland, with no visible window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wdraft
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTION ].\|.\|.
.RI [ FILE ].\|.\|.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wdraft
drags files into applications that only accept drag-and-drop, without opening
a window to drag from. Files are kept in a
.IR stash ;
you then put the pointer over the drop target and run
.B wdraft drop
from a compositor keybind, and the drop happens there. The pointer never moves
and nothing is drawn on screen.
.PP
It requires a Wayland compositor supporting
.B wlr-layer-shell
and
.BR wlr-virtual-pointer ,
which in practice means wlroots-based ones (sway, Hyprland, river, Wayfire,
labwc, niri). It is not an X11 program.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "add " "FILE.\|.\|." " | -"
Add files to the stash. A lone
.B -
reads one path per line from standard input. Paths are resolved to absolute and
must exist.
.TP
.BI "set " "FILE.\|.\|." " | -"
Replace the stash instead of appending to it.
.TP
.B list
Print the stash as
.B file://
URIs, or as plain paths with
.BR \-\-print\-path .
.TP
.B clear
Empty the stash.
.TP
.BI "drop " "[FILE.\|.\|.]"
Drop the stash onto whatever is under the pointer. With FILE arguments, drops
those instead and leaves the stash alone. On success the stash is cleared
unless
.B \-\-keep
is given.
.TP
.B catch
Print to standard output whatever is dropped anywhere on the screen. The whole
output becomes an invisible drop target, so you need not aim at a window.
.TP
.B copy
Put the stash on the clipboard as
.B text/uri-list
instead of dragging. Use this for targets that accept a paste but not a drop.
Backgrounds itself to retain clipboard ownership.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep
With
.BR drop ,
do not clear the stash after a successful drop.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-print\-path
Print filesystem paths instead of URIs
.RB ( list ", " catch ).
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-and\-exit
With
.BR catch ,
exit after one completed drop.
.TP
.BI \-t " MS" "\fR, \fP" \-\-timeout " MS"
Give up on a drop after MS milliseconds. Default 5000.
.TP
.BI \-s " MS" "\fR, \fP" \-\-settle " MS"
How long
.B drop
waits for the target to answer the drag before releasing the button. Default
600. Raise it for slow or heavily loaded targets; a target that has not
answered by then will not receive the drop.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Report what happens on standard error: cursor position, the button serial, the
MIME type negotiated, bytes transferred.
.TP
.B \-\-help
.TQ
.B \-\-version
Show usage or version and exit.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
The drop completed.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, or an empty stash.
.TP
.B 2
Nothing under the pointer accepted the drop. The stash is left alone.
.TP
.B 3
Timed out waiting for the drop to complete.
.TP
.B 4
No Wayland display, or the compositor lacks a required protocol.
.SH EXAMPLES
Stash a file, then drop it from a keybind. In your sway config:
.PP
.RS
.nf
bindsym $mod+d exec wdraft drop
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ wdraft add ~/photo.png
.fi
.RE
.PP
Then hover the upload area and press $mod+d.
.PP
To try it without a keybind, give yourself time to aim:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ wdraft add ~/photo.png && sleep 3 && wdraft -v drop
.fi
.RE
.PP
Receive files from another application:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ wdraft catch -p
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pipe a selection in, and keep it for several drops:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ find . -name '*.pdf' | wdraft set -
$ wdraft drop --keep
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
Wayland does not let a client start a drag out of nowhere:
.B wl_data_device.start_drag
needs a serial from a real button event on a surface the client owns. Nor do
the clipboard protocols help, as
.B ext-data-control
covers selections only.
.B wdraft
therefore maps a fully transparent fullscreen layer-shell surface to capture
the pointer where it already is, synthesises a left-button press on it with
.BR wlr-virtual-pointer ,
and once it holds the serial makes the surface input-transparent so the
compositor hands the drag to the real target underneath. Releasing the button
performs the drop.
.PP
Running
.B drop
from a terminal aims at the terminal. Use a keybind, or the
.B sleep
form above.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR wl-copy (1),
.BR swaymsg (1)
